  "notes": [
    "Door positions are lower halves at floor y=1; every custom door was one block above the floor and is removed by block_overrides so no duplicate/one-half doors remain.",
    "Backstage and parts/service openings are 2 blocks wide and 3 tall; standard 2-tall double leaves leave a 1-block transom gap above (no suitable 2x3 standard door exists in the new mod).",
    "Facing flips are applied to blocks whose new model base faces south while the old model base faced north (lockers, posters, hazard signs, desk, cardboard boxes, wall wires, neon sign, roof shingles).",
    "Window gets a per-cell layout connection mask instead of facing; layout values were derived from the new window model element patterns.",
    "Two framed 1-wide archways (opening x=23,z=15 and z=22,x=9) had no door in the old NBT and are intentionally left open; their frames become black trim blocks.",
    "The new big entrance is anchored at (12,1,32), not the old block y=2, so its 3-block height fills the opening rather than intersecting the facade lintel.",
    "Big entrance and custom doors use extra 'block'/'hinge' fields in the doors entries; they describe the intended new door block for runtimes that read them.",
    "Kitchen replaced management_wanted:big_employee_door with fnafmw:white_entrance_door (closest white standard door to the old white kitchen door)."
  ]
}
